class:: FadeDetection
summary:: Direction and fit of a rolling level fade
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Slope

description::
Fits RMS frame level in dB versus seconds using ordinary least squares. Returns a direction only when the absolute slope exceeds slopeThreshold and the coefficient of determination R.squared reaches minFit. Rising level gives +1, falling gives -1, otherwise zero. This describes the recent window rather than emitting a boundary trigger. The dB floor bounds silence. It is an independent regression descriptor.

Output starts after windowTime and updates every frameTime. Runtime is linear in the number of envelope frames, with no callback allocation. Vanilla Slope measures a local control derivative; FadeDetection fits a longer level trend and reports its goodness of fit.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: slopeThreshold
Nonnegative required absolute slope in dB/second.

argument:: minFit
Required R.squared from zero through one.

argument:: floorDB
Level floor, -160..0 dBFS.

returns::
Array [direction, slopeDBPerSecond, fit].

examples::
FadeDetection fits a linear regression line to rolling dB levels to detect whether sound is fading in (+1), fading out (-1), or stationary (0), qualified by a minimum goodness-of-fit threshold. In this example, detected fade-outs trigger an octave-up shimmer delay that swells musically as the primary note trails off. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time fade direction.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var fade = FadeDetection.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005, slopeThreshold: 5.0, minFit: 0.5);
        var dir = fade[0].lag(0.08);
        var fadeOutGate = (dir < -0.5).lag(0.02, 0.15);
        var shimmer = PitchShift.ar(source, 0.1, 2.0) * fadeOutGate * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (shimmer ! 2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, dir) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Fade Direction", ~miraBus, -1.0, 1.0, "dir");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
